  "title": "Forum stuck on 'Please wait for your files to be uploaded'",
  "content": "<p>  </p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/d07bcdd6-543b-40e2-87d3-d88642ac1f95.png\" /></figure><p>Nothing happened for ages; no animation of the ‘Create’ button.</p><p>I gave up, did a select-all and copy-paste to a new post in a new tab.</p><p>That one worked fine:</p><p><oembed url=\"https://community.st.com/feedback-forum-118/sidekick-wrong-on-c0-gpio-in-standby-167426\"></oembed></p><p> </p><p>Back at the original (still stuck “waiting”), I hit refresh, and it just went back to a blank form - all my edits lost and gone forever (if i hadn’t had the foresight to take a copy).</p><p> </p><p>See also:</p><p><oembed url=\"https://community.st.com/feedback-forum-118/something-s-gone-wrong-when-posting-a-reply-167168\"></oembed></p><p>But this time there was no error message - it just hung in that “waiting” state.</p><p> </p><p>Again, this is why we <u><strong>need</strong></u> the forum to save drafts!</p><oembed url=\"https://community.st.com/feedback-forum-118/forum-needs-to-save-drafts-166618\"></oembed><p> </p>",
